      "section": "6.8",
      "label": "(4)",
      "text": "All ﬁlled prescriptions (liquid, narcotic pain-killer dispensed by the hospital pharmacy) must be labeled at least visibly with 104\na. Patient name\nb. Drug code\nc. Name of drug\nd. Concentration\ne. Initial volume of drug\nf. Basal ﬂow rate\ng. VTBI\nh. Minimum time between bolus\ni. Date prescription ﬁlled\nj. Prescribing physician’s name\nk. Pharmacist name\nLabels may show additional information. Labels should be diﬃcult to counterfeit or modify without detection, only created and attached to ﬁlled prescriptions by a pharmacist in the hospital pharmacy. (UC1.7 §4.1.1)",
